{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"The divergence probe is too fragile to finish reliably (no majority-side leader that run), but it produced one useful, defensible observation: the minority leader acknowledged a client write. Let me submit that as a bounded check and keep divergence open."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_20-21-32-hashicorp_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport json\np='draft/update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['rationale']=(\\\"A follow-up probe extends the multi-voter scenario past the election, to the duty a client hands to that leader. After the isolated restarted node wins with two votes, a client Apply is issued on it and on the majority-side leader (if one exists), the partition is healed, and the two FSMs' applied slices are compared. The probe's bounded observation is that the minority leader accepted and completed the client write (minority_apply_ok true) even though its support is two of the committed five; the majority side had no leader in that run, so no two-sided conflict or FSM divergence was witnessed and none is claimed. This is submitted as a bounded check of the client-contract consequence: a write must not be acknowledged by a leader whose support is below the committed configuration's quorum. The established configuration-loss and minority-election findings are unchanged and not restated.\\\")\nd['sources']=[\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_restore_committed_body\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":724,\\\"end_line\\\":754,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_addvoter\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":994,\\\"end_line\\\":1005,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_apply_contract\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":245,\\\"end_line\\\":275,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"document_statement\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"raft_requestvote_leader_guard\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1690,\\\"end_line\\\":1700,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"raft_quorum_size\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1087,\\\"end_line\\\":1094,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"raft_electself_vote_count\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1999,\\\"end_line\\\":2060,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"fsm_apply_dispatch\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1245,\\\"end_line\\\":1295,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"}\n]\nd['experiment']={\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"9eb7105d2f8e48dfa54fcc262ad69cd9-question-0\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_restore_committed_body\\\",\\\"api_addvoter\\\",\\\"api_apply_contract\\\",\\\"raft_quorum_size\\\",\\\"raft_electself_vote_count\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Five-voter cluster whose leading node is restarted with RestoreCommittedLogs after a snapshot that predates the membership change, isolated together with one committed voter immediately after the restart. Once the isolated node is leader, a client Apply is issued on it and on the majority-side leader if one exists; the partition is then healed and the applied slices of both FSMs are compared. Run with the flag on and off.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"The isolated node's rebuilt configuration is the three-voter snapshot configuration, so its quorum is two while the committed configuration's quorum is three.\\\",\\\"An Apply that returns success is an acknowledged duty for the client.\\\",\\\"With the flag off the same isolation cannot produce a leader, so the write has no leader to succeed on.\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"Whole-package or repository test suites.\\\",\\\"Any FSM divergence or lost-entry claim; the probe did not produce a majority-side leader and such a claim needs both sides to write.\\\",\\\"The established configuration-loss and minority-election findings, which are recorded separately.\\\"],\n  \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"voters_before\\\":3,\\\"voters_after\\\":5,\\\"isolation\\\":\\\"immediately after restart\\\",\\\"apply_timeout_seconds\\\":2,\\\"heal_settle_seconds\\\":2}},\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"The harness reuses the same scenario construction as the immediate-isolation experiment (MakeClusterCustom with Peers 3, CommitTrackingLogs and RestoreCommittedLogs; a deliberate Snapshot; MakeClusterNoBootstrap(2) merged and two AddVoter calls; Shutdown and NewRaft on the same stores with a fresh inmem transport; Partition isolating the restarted node plus one committed voter with the pair reconnected). It then waits for the isolated node to become leader, issues Apply on it and on a majority-side leader when one exists, heals by reconnecting every transport, waits two seconds, and emits mvdiv_after_heal with the leadership outcome, both apply outcomes, the conflict index, the applied entries at that index where available, and the applied slice lengths; no production logic is modified.\\\",\n \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"The library owns the acknowledgement it gives a client: an Apply that reports success must rest on a majority of the committed configuration, which the caller cannot check from the public API.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"div_on\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"startup_before_restart\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"div_on\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"expected_servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":5}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"div_off\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"startup_before_restart\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"div_off\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"expected_servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":5}]}],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"mvdiv_after_heal\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"div_on\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"minority_apply_ok\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"restore_committed_logs\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"A client write must not be acknowledged on the isolated side, whose support is below the committed configuration's quorum; the defect prediction is that it is acknowledged.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"mvdiv_after_heal\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"div_off\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"minority_apply_ok\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"restore_committed_logs\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: with the committed configuration rebuilt the isolated side has no leader, so the write cannot be acknowledged there.\\\"}]}\nd['interpretations']=[\n {\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"9eb7105d2f8e48dfa54fcc262ad69cd9-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_apply_contract\\\",\\\"raft_quorum_size\\\",\\\"raft_electself_vote_count\\\",\\\"api_restore_committed_body\\\"],\n  \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"conditional\\\",\\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Source: an Apply is acknowledged once the entry is committed and applied (api.go's Apply contract at 245-275 with the leader's commit path), and commitment is computed from the leader's configuration view; with the stale three-server list quorumSize() (raft.go:1087-1094) returns two, so the isolated node's own vote plus one follower is enough to commit a client write. A native run of the probe showed exactly that: the isolated node became leader (minority_leader true) and its Apply returned success (minority_apply_ok true), i.e. a client would receive an acknowledgement for a write supported by two of the committed five voters. The same run had no majority-side leader, so no conflicting entry and no FSM divergence was observed, and none is claimed. The submitted experiment re-runs both modes for a receipt; only its receipt can complete the comparison.\\\",\n  \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\\\"The flag-off control cannot produce a leader on the isolated side, so the acknowledgement is tied to the stale configuration rather than to the partition alone.\\\",\\\"The probe did not achieve a two-sided write, so the stronger lost-entry consequence is not established.\\\"],\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"No receipt yet for the client-contract check; the account rests on source reading plus one native probe.\\\",\\\"FSM divergence and lost acknowledged entries are not witnessed; the majority side had no leader in the probe.\\\",\\\"Bounded waits are used throughout, so no occurrence-rate or absence is claimed.\\\"]}]\nit=d['interpretations'][0] if False else None\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=2)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_20-21-32-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
