},\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"The harness reuses the same scenario construction as the immediate-isolation experiment (MakeClusterCustom with Peers 3, CommitTrackingLogs and RestoreCommittedLogs; a deliberate Snapshot; MakeClusterNoBootstrap(2) merged and two AddVoter calls; Shutdown and NewRaft on the same stores with a fresh inmem transport; Partition isolating the restarted node plus one committed voter with the pair reconnected). It then waits for the isolated node to become leader, issues Apply on it and on a majority-side leader when one exists, heals by reconnecting every transport, waits two seconds, and emits mvdiv_after_heal with the leadership outcome, both apply outcomes, the conflict index, the applied entries at that index where available, and the applied slice lengths; no production logic is modified.\\\",\n \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"The library owns the acknowledgement it gives a client: an Apply that reports success must rest on a majority of the committed configuration, which the caller cannot check from the public API.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"div_on\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"startup_before_restart\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"div_on\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"expected_servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":5}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"div_off\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"startup_before_restart\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"div_off\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"expected_servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":5}]}],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"mvdiv_after_heal\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"div_on\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"minority_apply_ok\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"restore_committed_logs\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"A client write must not be acknowledged on the isolated side, whose support is below the committed configuration's quorum; the defect prediction is that it is acknowledged.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"mvdiv_after_heal\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"div_off\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"minority_apply_ok\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"restore_committed_logs\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: with the committed configuration rebuilt the isolated side has no leader, so the write cannot be acknowledged there.\\\"}]}\nd['interpretations']=[\n {\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"9eb7105d2f8e48dfa54fcc262ad69cd9-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_apply_contract\\\",\\\"raft_quorum_size\\\",\\\"raft_electself_vote_count\\\",\\\"api_restore_committed_body\\\"],\n  \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"conditional\\\",\\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Source: an Apply is acknowledged once the entry is committed and applied (api.go's Apply contract at 245-275 with the leader's commit path), and commitment is computed from the leader's configuration view; with the stale three-server list quorumSize() (raft.go:1087-1094) returns two, so the isolated node's own vote plus one follower is enough to commit a client write. A native run of the probe showed exactly that: the isolated node became leader (minority_leader true) and its Apply returned success (minority_apply_ok true), i.e. a client would receive an acknowledgement for a write supported by two of the committed five voters. The same run had no majority-side leader, so no conflicting entry and no FSM divergence was observed, and none is claimed. The submitted experiment re-runs both modes for a receipt; only its receipt can complete the comparison.\\\",\n  \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\\\"The flag-off control cannot produce a leader on the isolated side, so the acknowledgement is tied to the stale configuration rather than to the partition alone.\\\",\\\"The probe did not achieve a two-sided write, so the stronger lost-entry consequence is not established.\\\"],\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"No receipt yet for the client-contract check; the account rests on source reading plus one native probe.\\\",\\\"FSM divergence and lost acknowledged entries are not witnessed; the majority side had no leader in the probe.\\\",\\\"Bounded waits are used throughout, so no occurrence-rate or absence is claimed.\\\"]}]\nit=d['interpretations'][0] if False else None\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=2)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_20-21-32-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"ok\n{\"valid\": true, \"run_id\": \"81876a26fa4a40c997892d2ca473cab3\", \"elapsed_seconds\": 1991.656534558002, \"diagnostics\": [], \"meaning\": \"Read-only validation of these bytes and saved state; no acceptance, execution or budget reservation\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
