{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_20-21-32-hashicorp_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport json\np='draft/update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['interpretations']=[{\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"9eb7105d2f8e48dfa54fcc262ad69cd9-question-0\\\",\n \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"c34a830a404a4dad8ea4e2fe492f5e66-experiment\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_restore_committed_call\\\",\\\"api_restore_committed_body\\\",\\\"api_addvoter\\\",\\\"api_apply_contract\\\",\\\"raft_requestvote_leader_guard\\\",\\\"raft_quorum_size\\\",\\\"raft_electself_vote_count\\\"],\n \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"abfdbd1823b342409ef4a815bade0407\\\":[21,22,24,25],\\\"b15f4b6c55b44402ace926204de9b826\\\":[15,18]},\n \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"violated\\\",\\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Two completed comparisons answer this question, each with its flag-off control, and a third consequence is under test. Configuration: receipt b15f4b6c55b44402ace926204de9b826, comparison 0 violated at witness event index 15 - the node restarted from a log whose latest configuration is index 14 with five servers came back at configuration index 1 with three servers, the snapshot's bootstrap configuration - with the control holding at evaluated event index 18 (index 14, five servers). Election: receipt abfdbd1823b342409ef4a815bade0407, comparison 0 violated at witness event index 22 - the restarted node, isolated together with one committed voter immediately after NewRaft returned, became leader with reachable_votes 2 against committed_quorum 3, and the same run reports majority_side_leader true, so a leader elected on a minority of the committed configuration coexisted with the majority side's leader - with the control holding at evaluated event index 25 (became_leader false). Source: restoreFromCommittedLogs (api.go:724-754) advances lastApplied to the persisted commit index before the startup scan at api.go:604-620, so AddVoter's later entry (api.go:994-1005) is never re-read and the node keeps the snapshot's three-server list; quorumSize() (raft.go:1087-1094) then returns two and electSelf (raft.go:1999-2060) asks only that list, so the node's own vote plus one follower meets its stale quorum while the committed configuration needs three. The manouevre the run needed - also cutting the single committed voter off from the majority side so requestVote's existing-leader guard (raft.go:1690-1700) does not refuse the vote - is an ordinary partition shape; two executions produced the minority leadership and two settled-schedule executions did not, so the manifestation is schedule dependent while the decision itself is unrepaired. Third, the duty a client hands to such a leader is being checked: in a native run of the extended probe the isolated leader accepted and completed a client Apply (minority_apply_ok true) with two of five committed votes in support, which the submitted comparison now tests against its control; no divergence or lost-entry claim is made, because that run had no majority-side leader to write against.\\\",\n \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\\\"The flag-off controls in both receipts keep the committed configuration and cannot win on the isolated side.\\\",\\\"Two settled-schedule executions did not produce the minority win, and the difference is explained by whether the isolated partner still heard the majority-side leader, so no frequency claim is made.\\\",\\\"The redundant configuration re-checks in one receipt were incomplete because the two scenarios emit the same restart event name; they carry no new claim and are not used.\\\"],\n \\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"Only the leadership decision, the coexistence with the majority-side leader and (in a native probe) the acknowledgement of a client write are observed; no FSM divergence or lost acknowledged entry is witnessed.\\\",\\\"Observed windows are bounded, so no occurrence-rate or absence bound is established.\\\",\\\"The scenario restarts the former leader of an enlarged cluster; other roles, change types and chain orders are not explored.\\\"],\n \\\"answers\\\":{\\\"7da03e78394f41fdad540ae0824ec2a6-gap-1\\\":{\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The election part is resolved by a complete comparison: receipt abfdbd1823b342409ef4a815bade0407, comparison 0 violated at witness event index 22 (leader with two votes against a committed quorum of three, co-existing with the majority-side leader) and its control holding at index 25. Reproduction depends on whether the single committed voter on the isolated side still hears the majority-side leader, because requestVote refuses candidates while a leader is known (raft.go:1690-1700); with immediate isolation it reproduced twice, with the settled schedule it did not. Entry-level divergence between the two leaders remains unwitnessed - the extended probe found no majority-side leader - so the gap stays open on that point.\\\",\\\"resolved\\\":False}},\n \\\"joint_history\\\":\\\"Receipt b15f4b6c55b44402ace926204de9b826 supplies the configuration comparison and receipt abfdbd1823b342409ef4a815bade0407 supplies the election comparison; both are complete executions of the same five-voter scenario over identical stores, sizes and snapshot timing, and both report the same configuration values (index 1 with three servers against expected 14 with five, controls at 14 with five). They are separate complete histories rather than fragments: each built its own cluster, and only the comparison declarations and result event names differ between them.\\\"}]\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=2)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_20-21-32-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
